    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0280" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg192"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Phelps.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic">June 10,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 433.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 447, of the 22d ultimo, concerning the protection of American
                    inventors in Germany.</p>
                <p>The Department’s No. 420, of May 19, 1892, sufficiently answers the further
                    statements of the imperial secretary of state for foreign affairs, in relation
                    to the nonpublication of the notification in question, pending the conclusion of
                    a trade-mark treaty which will definitely adjust the matter.</p>
                <p>I am, sir,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
